// The depth guard's LOWER side, pinned. `json_render_guard.nova` pins that
// one level past `MAX_RENDER_DEPTH` panics; nothing before this fixture
// pinned that legitimate input well within the bound still renders.
//
// This does NOT pin the exact bound -- it pins that the bound is not below
// 99999, which is a weaker claim. A mutation that lowered
// `MAX_RENDER_DEPTH` to, say, 100 would make this fixture fail without this
// fixture ever having measured where between 100 and 100000 the real edge
// sits. Only `json_render_guard.nova`, together with this one, pins the
// edge itself, and only because the two together bracket it at
// `MAX_RENDER_DEPTH` exactly (100001 panics, 99999 renders).
//
// Depth chosen as `MAX_RENDER_DEPTH - 1` = 99999, one below the guard's
// panic threshold, so the two fixtures bracket the same boundary from
// opposite sides. Measured against this build: renders in about 2.1
// seconds.
fn main() {
    let mut v = Number(1.0)
    let mut i = 0
    while i < 99999 {
        v = Array([v])
        i = i + 1
    }
    println("built, about to render")
    println("${stringify(v).len()}")
}
